From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:37:14 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/30] SWGL: blend functions without a CPU key are fine when a
 GPU blends

Hiding the KHR advanced equations sends WebRender's mix-blend-mode down
its shader path, whose blend functions the CPU rasterizer's key table does
not list; the assertion took wrench down on blend/large.yaml. With a
device attached the GPU blends them, and the CPU key falls back to none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gfx/wr/swgl/src/gl.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gfx/wr/swgl/src/gl.cc b/gfx/wr/swgl/src/gl.cc
index d2d4fcce19..084e5b6673 100644
--- a/gfx/wr/swgl/src/gl.cc
+++ b/gfx/wr/swgl/src/gl.cc
@@ -1448,7 +1448,11 @@ static void hash_blend_key() {
     default:
       debugf("blendfunc: %x, %x, separate: %x, %x, equation: %x\n", srgb, drgb,
              sa, da, equation);
-      assert(false);
+      // With a GPU shading the pixels, WebRender may pick blend functions the
+      // CPU rasterizer has no key for (mix-blend-mode without the advanced
+      // equations); the GPU blends whatever GL can express.
+      assert(ctx->gpu);
+      ctx->blend_key = BLEND_KEY_NONE;
       break;
   }
 }
